## PrintFriendly API
> Turn a web page, HTML or Markdown into a PDF, Word, Markdown, JSON, HTML or text file with the PrintFriendly HTML to PDF API, or through an MCP server for AI agents.
- [HTML to PDF API](https://www.printfriendly.com/api): REST API that turns any web page, HTML or Markdown into a clean PDF, Word, Markdown or JSON document, with a free plan and an MCP server for AI agents.
- [API documentation (v2)](https://www.printfriendly.com/api/instructions/v2): Reference for the REST API: authentication, endpoints (pdf, html and text), every parameter, response and error codes, limits, and code samples in curl, Python, and Node.js.
- Get a free API key at https://www.printfriendly.com/me/api-key: free API key, 100 documents a month, no credit card, send it as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
- Check a key at GET https://api.printfriendly.com/v2/usage: free, does not use a document. Answers 200 with the plan, documents used, included and remaining, even when the key's allowance is used up.
- [OpenAPI description](https://www.printfriendly.com/openapi.json): OpenAPI 3.1 spec for POST /v2/convert (URL, HTML or Markdown to PDF, Word, Markdown, JSON, HTML or text) and the older create endpoints, with every error code.
- [PrintFriendly API in Postman](https://www.postman.com/printfriendly/printfriendly-api): Public workspace with every endpoint, ready to run. Set the `bearerToken` variable to your key, then send GET /v2/usage.
- [Full API reference for agents](https://www.printfriendly.com/llms-full.txt): The whole API in plain text: authentication, the convert endpoint with curl examples, error codes and limits.
## PrintFriendly for AI assistants
> Use PrintFriendly from Claude and other AI assistants, or send a person to a clean page with a plain link.
- [PrintFriendly connector for Claude and other AI assistants](https://www.printfriendly.com/api/mcp): MCP connector address. Add it as a connector to print a web page or make a PDF from a chat.
- [Using PrintFriendly in AI assistants](https://www.printfriendly.com/help/ai-assistants): How to add the connector to any assistant that connects to MCP servers.
- [Using PrintFriendly in Claude](https://www.printfriendly.com/help/claude): How to add the connector to Claude.
- [PrintFriendly MCP server for developers](https://www.printfriendly.com/help/api-mcp): Remote MCP server at https://mcp.printfriendly.com for Claude Code, Cursor, VS Code and your own agents. Send an API key as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`; tools read_page (a page as clean Markdown) and create_document (PDF, Word, Markdown, HTML, JSON or plain text).
- Any assistant or app can link a person to `https://www.printfriendly.com/print?url=<url-encoded page url>` to open a clean, printable, ad-free version of that page. No account or API key is needed.
